// src/argv_dispatch.pdx — cat.M1-001..M1-003 (skeleton) → cat.M2-001..M2-004
// → cat.M3-001..M3-003 → v1.1-A retirement → v1.2.0-A (Closes #25)
// CatDispatch module: argv → parsed flags + positional list → per-
// file streaming read → (render-text OR semantic-pipe) → TtySink;
// OR stdin read → render → TtySink when argv has zero positionals.
//
// v1.2.0-A retirement note (Closes cat #25 — libpdx-argv migration)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// cat_parse_argv (the hand-rolled inline byte scanner defined below)
// is RETIRED in the live path by the v1.1-A substrate flip: _start
// in src/entry.pdx handles its own argv walk directly (byte-through
// only — no -n / -A / --schema at v1.1-A) and never calls
// cat_dispatch or cat_parse_argv. deps.list at v1.2.0-A declares
// `libpdx-argv >= 1.1.3` and src/tool_ident.pdx defines the
// PDX_TOOL_NAME + PDX_TOOL_VERSION externs required by the
// libpdx-argv v1.1.3 VersionBackend::emit_default contract
// (paideia-os/libpdx-argv #42). The v1.1-C follow-up rewires
// _start's inline `--version` compare + the future flag-layer
// resurrection through Parser::parse_argv_ex, at which point the
// symbols and control paths in THIS module are removable outright
// alongside the sibling stub cleanups tracked in the tty_sink.pdx
// header note.
//
// Until then, cat_parse_argv / cat_reset / cat_dispatch / the
// PARSE_ERR_* / FLAG_* / POS_MAX constants below remain in tree so
// tests/*.pdx (which still reference these symbols but never link
// into cat.elf) continue to compile.
//
// M3 pipeline (extends M2 with audit-first + semantic-pipe layer)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Per-invocation prelude (steps 1–4 unchanged from M2). Per-file
// loop (step 5 file-path branch) gains two new stages:
//
//   5a. audit_stub_file_read(pos_ptrs[i]) — M3-003. Journals a
//       FileReadRecord to /system/audit/user-events/ BEFORE the
//       first byte of this file reaches the sink. On broker
//       unreachable → CAT_EXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR (3). This is the D3
//       audit-first gate: a tool that cannot journal its output
//       must not emit output.
//
//   5b. Branch on FLAG_SCHEMA (bit 2 of flag_mask):
//         - FLAG_SCHEMA clear → M2 render path unchanged:
//           chunked file_read_chunk → render_write_bytes →
//           tty_write_byte(s).
//         - FLAG_SCHEMA set → file_schema_query(handle):
//             - hash_ptr != 0 → M3-001 schema-typed passthrough:
//               chunked file_read_chunk →
//               pipe_forward_write(hash_ptr, fr_chunk_buf, bytes).
//               The per-chunk write fans out into ≤ 4056-byte
//               framed records on the semantic-pipe wire.
//             - hash_ptr == 0 → M3-002 RawByteChunk emission:
//               rbc_reset (zeros per-file offset + installs hash),
//               chunked file_read_chunk → rbc_emit_chunk which
//               composes [offset:u64 | bytes] records ≤ 4048 body
//               bytes each and calls pipe_forward_frame per
//               record.
//
// Stdin path (pos_count == 0) is unchanged from M2 — no per-file
// audit (there is no file) and no schema branch (stdin carries
// no `.pdxfs` metadata).
//
// M2 pipeline (baseline, unchanged where not overridden by M3)
// ------------------------------------------------------------
//   1. `cat_reset` — zero parser state.
//   2. `cat_parse_argv` — populate `flag_mask`, `pos_ptrs`,
//      `pos_count`. Parse error collapses to CAT_EXIT_USAGE_ERROR.
//   3. `tty_reset` — zero sink cursor.
//   4. `render_reset(flag_mask)` — save flags, init line counter
//      to 1, mark at-line-start. Continuity of line numbering
//      across concatenated files is preserved because reset runs
//      once BEFORE the per-file loop.
//   5. Branch on pos_count:
//        - pos_count == 0 → stdin path (M2-004): loop
//          `stdin_read_chunk(fr_chunk_buf, CHUNK_MAX)` →
//          `render_write_bytes(fr_chunk_buf, bytes)` until EOF
//          (0-byte read).
//        - pos_count > 0 → multi-file path (M2-001, extended by
//          M3 as above).
//   6. Return CAT_EXIT_OK / CAT_EXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR (any sink
//      overflow, audit unreachable) / CAT_EXIT_CAP_DENIED (any
//      file_open miss).
//
// Streaming discipline (M2-003)
// -----------------------------
// The per-source read loop uses `FileRead::fr_chunk_buf` — a
// 64 KiB `.bss` scratch buffer — as the staging area. Both
// `file_read_chunk` and `stdin_read_chunk` cap their per-call byte
// count at CHUNK_MAX = 65536 so the working set is bounded at 64
// KiB independent of file size. A 1 GiB file is streamed through
// 16384 chunks; RAM never holds more than one chunk.
//
// Test seedability (M4 sets up state before dispatch)
// ---------------------------------------------------
// `cat_dispatch` does NOT call `file_read_reset` / `stdin_reset`
// / `audit_stub_reset` / `file_schema_reset` itself — those clear
// the M2/M3 seed tables which the M4 test harness populates
// BEFORE dispatch (via `file_read_seed_push`, `stdin_seed`,
// `audit_stub_seed_broker_failure`, `file_schema_seed`). This
// lets a test seed once, dispatch, and inspect
// `TtySink::tty_out_buf` plus `audit_stub_get_count` +
// `rbc_get_offset`. Real R42 / libpdx-audit / libpdx-semantic-
// pipe wiring replaces the seed tables with `sys_pdxfs_open`,
// `sys_ipc_send` (audit journal), and `Passthrough::pipe_forward`;
// the M3 stub helpers are deleted at that point and
// `cat_dispatch`'s own control flow does not change.
//
// Exit-code discipline (per I4 in design/tooling/plan.md §4.2):
//   0 — every file read and rendered successfully
//   2 — usage error (parse error, positional overflow)
//   3 — system error (render sink overflow, propagated from
//        tty_write_byte / tty_write_bytes; R42 will add file-read
//        I/O errors on the same code)
//   4 — cap denied / file not found (file_open miss)
//
// paideia-as compliance
// ---------------------
//   - Module name PascalCase basename (`CatDispatch`), no directory
//     prefix.
//   - No `test` mnemonic; every zero-check via `cmp reg, 0`.
//   - Every `cmp reg, imm` uses immediate ≤ 0x7FFFFFFF (M2's
//     largest: 65536 for CHUNK_MAX / TTY_OUT_CAP; 255 for
//     NAME_MAX_LEN in the argv parser body -- matches the
//     kernel PATH_MAX ceiling, ENH-009 / #19).
//   - r11 scratch (paideia-as reserved); reloaded before every
//     `.bss` read/write.
//   - Byte reads use `xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [ptr]` (#1248).
//   - SysV push/pop parity: `cat_dispatch` uses a 5-push callee-
//     save prologue (rbx / r12 / r13 / r14 / r15) — rsp%16 == 0
//     at every nested call site.
//   - Instruction vocabulary stays inside the R49 reference-
//     implementation subset (see design/architecture.md §5).

module ArgvDispatch = structure {

  // ============================================================================
  // Exit codes (per I4 collapsed vocabulary)
  // ============================================================================
  pub let CAT_EXIT_OK               : u64 = 0
  pub let CAT_EXIT_USAGE_ERROR      : u64 = 2
  pub let CAT_EXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR     : u64 = 3
  pub let CAT_EXIT_CAP_DENIED       : u64 = 4

  // ============================================================================
  // Parser return codes (internal to cat_parse_argv). Collapsed to
  // CAT_EXIT_USAGE_ERROR by cat_dispatch for the process exit.
  // ============================================================================
  pub let PARSE_OK                          : u64 = 0
  pub let PARSE_ERR_UNKNOWN_LONG_FLAG       : u64 = 1
  pub let PARSE_ERR_UNKNOWN_OR_CLUSTERED_SHORT : u64 = 2
  pub let PARSE_ERR_POS_OVERFLOW            : u64 = 3
  pub let PARSE_ERR_LONG_MISSING_NAME       : u64 = 4
  pub let PARSE_ERR_NAME_TOO_LONG           : u64 = 5

  // ============================================================================
  // Flag bit mask constants (mirror Render::RENDER_FLAG_*)
  // ============================================================================
  pub let FLAG_N       : u64 = 0x1   // -n      line numbering (M2-002)
  pub let FLAG_A       : u64 = 0x2   // -A      non-printable render (M2-002)
  pub let FLAG_SCHEMA  : u64 = 0x4   // --schema schema records (M3)

  // ============================================================================
  // Argv-parse limits
  // ============================================================================
  pub let NAME_MAX_LEN : u64 = 255
  pub let POS_MAX      : u64 = 8

  // ============================================================================
  // Singleton .bss (bootstrap-scope; M4 migrates to caller-owned)
  // ============================================================================
  pub let mut flag_mask : u64 = uninit @align(8)
  pub let mut pos_ptrs : [u64; 8] = uninit @align(8)
  pub let mut pos_count : u64 = uninit @align(8)
  pub let mut parse_error_arg_index : u64 = uninit @align(8)

  // ============================================================================
  // cat_reset()
  //
  // Signature: cat_reset : () -> () !{mem} @{}
  //
  // Zero flag_mask, pos_count, parse_error_arg_index. Leaf; r11
  // scratch; no push/pop parity.
  // ============================================================================
  pub let cat_reset : () -> () !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "cat.M1-002 cat_reset. Zero flag_mask, pos_count, parse_error_arg_index so a subsequent cat_parse_argv starts from a known baseline. Leaf function; r11 scratch used only for the .bss lea; no callee-save touched.",
      block: {
        xor rax, rax;
        lea r11, [rip + flag_mask];              mov [r11], rax;
        lea r11, [rip + pos_count];              mov [r11], rax;
        lea r11, [rip + parse_error_arg_index];  mov [r11], rax;
        ret;
      }
    }

  // ============================================================================
  // cat_parse_argv(argv, argc) -> rc
  //
  // Signature: cat_parse_argv : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{}
  //   RDI: argv (u64* — array of NUL-terminated arg pointers)
  //   RSI: argc (count of entries in argv)
  //   RAX: PARSE_OK on success, else one of the PARSE_ERR_* codes.
  //        On error, parse_error_arg_index is set to the offending
  //        argv index.
  //
  // See design/architecture.md §2 for the full grammar. Preserved
  // verbatim from M1 (libpdx-argv M2 has since landed FKIND_UNKNOWN
  // = 0xFF returning as boolean, which would let us migrate; the
  // migration is scheduled at cat.M3 in the plan so the M2 wave
  // stays byte-compatible with the M1 fixtures).
  // ============================================================================
  pub let cat_parse_argv : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (argv: u64) (argc: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "cat.M1-002 cat_parse_argv. Preserved verbatim across the M2 wave — libpdx-argv M2's FKIND_UNKNOWN=boolean fix removes the original blocker, but migrating cat's argv surface to libpdx-argv is scheduled at cat.M3 per r49-r50-plan.md §5.5 so the M2 wave keeps byte-compat with the M1 golden fixtures. Walks argv[1..argc-1]; classifies each arg as long-flag / short-flag / positional per design/architecture.md §2 grammar. Boolean-only flags (arity 0 — a shell that wrote 'cat -n foo.txt' means cat reads foo.txt, not that -n's value is foo.txt). Long-flag whitelist: --schema only (byte-exact compare). Short-flag whitelist: -n and -A. Positional accumulator uses pos_ptrs[pos_count] and enforces POS_MAX = 8. Every positional walked to NUL with NAME_MAX_LEN = 255 bound (ENH-009, #19 -- matches the kernel PATH_MAX ceiling). All immediates in `cmp reg, imm` are ≤ 0x7FFFFFFF (max 255). Every byte load preceded by xor rax,rax (#1248). Leaf function.",
      block: {
        mov r9, rdi;
        mov r10, rsi;
        mov r8, 1;

      cat_parse_loop_head:
        cmp r8, r10;
        jge cat_parse_done_ok;

        mov rdx, [r9 + r8*8];

        xor rax, rax;
        mov_b rax, [rdx];
        cmp rax, 0x2D;
        je cat_parse_maybe_flag;
        jmp cat_parse_positional;

      cat_parse_maybe_flag:
        xor rax, rax;
        mov_b rax, [rdx + 1];
        cmp rax, 0x2D;
        je cat_parse_long_flag;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je cat_parse_positional;
        jmp cat_parse_short_flag;

      cat_parse_long_flag:
        xor rax, rax;
        mov_b rax, [rdx + 2];
        cmp rax, 0;
        je cat_parse_long_missing;
        cmp rax, 0x3D;
        je cat_parse_long_missing;

        xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [rdx + 2]; cmp rax, 0x73; jne cat_parse_unknown_long;
        xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [rdx + 3]; cmp rax, 0x63; jne cat_parse_unknown_long;
        xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [rdx + 4]; cmp rax, 0x68; jne cat_parse_unknown_long;
        xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [rdx + 5]; cmp rax, 0x65; jne cat_parse_unknown_long;
        xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [rdx + 6]; cmp rax, 0x6D; jne cat_parse_unknown_long;
        xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [rdx + 7]; cmp rax, 0x61; jne cat_parse_unknown_long;
        xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [rdx + 8]; cmp rax, 0;    jne cat_parse_unknown_long;

        lea r11, [rip + flag_mask];
        mov rax, [r11];
        or  rax, 0x4;
        mov [r11], rax;
        jmp cat_parse_advance;

      cat_parse_unknown_long:
        mov rax, 1;
        jmp cat_parse_fail;

      cat_parse_long_missing:
        mov rax, 4;
        jmp cat_parse_fail;

      cat_parse_short_flag:
        xor rax, rax;
        mov_b rax, [rdx + 2];
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne cat_parse_unknown_short;

        xor rax, rax;
        mov_b rax, [rdx + 1];
        cmp rax, 0x6E;
        je cat_parse_short_n;
        cmp rax, 0x41;
        je cat_parse_short_A;
        jmp cat_parse_unknown_short;

      cat_parse_short_n:
        lea r11, [rip + flag_mask];
        mov rax, [r11];
        or  rax, 0x1;
        mov [r11], rax;
        jmp cat_parse_advance;

      cat_parse_short_A:
        lea r11, [rip + flag_mask];
        mov rax, [r11];
        or  rax, 0x2;
        mov [r11], rax;
        jmp cat_parse_advance;

      cat_parse_unknown_short:
        mov rax, 2;
        jmp cat_parse_fail;

      cat_parse_positional:
        mov rcx, rdx;
        xor rax, rax;
        xor r11, r11;

      cat_parse_pos_measure_head:
        cmp r11, 255;                    // NAME_MAX_LEN (ENH-009, #19)
        jg cat_parse_name_too_long;

        xor rax, rax;
        mov_b rax, [rcx];
        cmp rax, 0;
        je cat_parse_pos_measure_done;
        add rcx, 1;
        add r11, 1;
        jmp cat_parse_pos_measure_head;

      cat_parse_pos_measure_done:
        cmp r11, 0;
        je cat_parse_empty_pos;

        lea r11, [rip + pos_count];
        mov rax, [r11];
        cmp rax, 8;
        jge cat_parse_pos_overflow;

        lea r11, [rip + pos_ptrs];
        mov [r11 + rax*8], rdx;

        add rax, 1;
        lea r11, [rip + pos_count];
        mov [r11], rax;
        jmp cat_parse_advance;

      cat_parse_empty_pos:
        mov rax, 3;
        jmp cat_parse_fail;

      cat_parse_pos_overflow:
        mov rax, 3;
        jmp cat_parse_fail;

      cat_parse_name_too_long:
        mov rax, 5;
        jmp cat_parse_fail;

      cat_parse_advance:
        add r8, 1;
        jmp cat_parse_loop_head;

      cat_parse_fail:
        lea r11, [rip + parse_error_arg_index];
        mov [r11], r8;
        ret;

      cat_parse_done_ok:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret;
      }
    }

  // ============================================================================
  // cat_dispatch(argv, argc) -> exit_code
  //
  // Signature: cat_dispatch : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{}
  //   RDI: argv
  //   RSI: argc
  //   RAX: exit code (0 / 2 / 3 / 4 per I4)
  //
  // M2 top-level: parse argv → set up render + sink → stream every
  // positional file (or stdin when pos_count == 0) through the
  // render pipeline into the sink. See file header for the full
  // flow.
  //
  // Register plan (5-push callee-save prologue for 16-byte align):
  //   rbx = current file handle (across file_read_chunk calls)
  //   r12 = argv (initial); reused after parse for scratch
  //   r13 = argc (initial); reused after parse for pos_count snapshot
  //   r14 = current positional index i (file loop)
  //   r15 = alignment pad (unused)
  //   rax = byte load / call return
  //   rcx = scratch
  //   rdi/rsi/rdx = call args
  //   r11 = lea scratch (paideia-as reserved)
  //
  // rsp arithmetic: entry rsp%16 == 8 (post-CALL). 5 pushes lands
  // rsp%16 == 0 at every nested call site.
  // ============================================================================
  pub let cat_dispatch : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (argv: u64) (argc: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "cat.M2-001..M2-004 + cat.M3-001..M3-003 cat_dispatch. Sequences cat_reset → cat_parse_argv → tty_reset → render_reset(flag_mask) → branch on pos_count → per-file streaming (or stdin streaming). Per-file loop gains two M3 stages: (5a) audit_stub_file_read(pos_ptrs[i]) before first byte — journals a FileReadRecord; broker unreachable → CAT_EXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR (3); (5b) FLAG_SCHEMA branch — clear routes to the M2 render_write_bytes path unchanged; set routes to file_schema_query(handle) which returns hash_ptr (0 = schemaless): non-zero hash → pipe_forward_write(hash, chunk, bytes) per chunk (M3-001 schema-typed passthrough via semantic-pipe framed records); zero hash → rbc_reset then rbc_emit_chunk(chunk, bytes) per chunk (M3-002 RawByteChunk emission, per-file offset advanced internally). Streaming loop uses FileRead::fr_chunk_buf (64 KiB .bss) as staging area — file_read_chunk / stdin_read_chunk cap per-call bytes at CHUNK_MAX = 65536, and cat_dispatch loops until EOF (0-byte read). Every nested call return checked: parse failure → CAT_EXIT_USAGE_ERROR (2); render_write_bytes / pipe_forward_write / rbc_emit_chunk non-zero → CAT_EXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR (3); audit_stub_file_read non-zero → CAT_EXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR (3); file_open == 0 → CAT_EXIT_CAP_DENIED (4). file_close return ignored (M2 no-op; R42 close-fail becomes CAT_EXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR — a body-only edit at that time). 5-push callee-save prologue (rbx / r12 / r13 / r14 / r15) lands rsp%16 == 0 at every nested call site. Register plan: rbx = current file handle; r12 = M3 schema hash ptr for current file (0 = RBC path); r13 = pos_count snapshot (after parse); r14 = file-loop index i; r15 = alignment pad. All `cmp reg, imm` immediates ≤ 0x7FFFFFFF (65536 largest for CHUNK_MAX). cat_dispatch does NOT reset FileRead / StdinSource / AuditStub / FileSchema seed tables — those are stub-only test state the M4 harness sets up BEFORE calling cat_dispatch (see file header for the R42/libpdx wiring note that removes seed tables entirely). RawByteChunk::rbc_reset IS called per-file inside the RBC-path arm because it zeroes the per-file byte offset (starts at 0 for each file per M3-002 spec).",
      block: {
        // ---- prologue: 5 pushes for 16-byte alignment -----------------
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;
        push r14;
        push r15;

        mov r12, rdi;                   // r12 = argv
        mov r13, rsi;                   // r13 = argc

        // ---- Step 1: reset parser state -------------------------------
        call cat_reset;

        // ---- Step 2: parse argv ---------------------------------------
        mov rdi, r12;
        mov rsi, r13;
        call cat_parse_argv;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne cd_usage_error;

        // ---- Step 3: reset sink + render state ------------------------
        call tty_reset;

        // render_reset(flag_mask)
        lea r11, [rip + flag_mask];
        mov rdi, [r11];
        call render_reset;

        // ---- Step 4: load pos_count snapshot into r13 -----------------
        // (argc no longer needed; reuse r13.)
        lea r11, [rip + pos_count];
        mov r13, [r11];

        // Branch on pos_count.
        cmp r13, 0;
        je cd_stdin_path;
        jmp cd_file_path;

        // ==============================================================
        //   File path (M2-001 multi-file + M2-003 streaming +
        //   M3-001 schema-typed passthrough + M3-002 RawByteChunk +
        //   M3-003 per-file FileReadRecord audit)
        // ==============================================================
      cd_file_path:
        xor r14, r14;                   // i = 0

      cd_file_outer_head:
        cmp r14, r13;
        jge cd_ok;

        // ---- file_open(pos_ptrs[r14]) --------------------------------
        lea r11, [rip + pos_ptrs];
        mov rdi, [r11 + r14*8];
        call file_open;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je cd_cap_denied;
        mov rbx, rax;                   // rbx = handle

        // ---- M3-003: audit_stub_file_read(pos_ptrs[r14]) --------------
        // MUST land before any byte of this file's output reaches the
        // sink. On broker unreachable → CAT_EXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR (3) per
        // D3 audit-first (see plan §3).
        lea r11, [rip + pos_ptrs];
        mov rdi, [r11 + r14*8];
        call audit_stub_file_read;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne cd_system_error;

        // ---- Branch on FLAG_SCHEMA (bit 2 of flag_mask) --------------
        lea r11, [rip + flag_mask];
        mov rax, [r11];
        and rax, 0x4;                   // FLAG_SCHEMA
        cmp rax, 0;
        je cd_file_render_path;

        // ---- M3 schema path: query per-file schema hash --------------
        mov rdi, rbx;
        call file_schema_query;
        mov r12, rax;                   // r12 = hash_ptr (0 = schemaless)

        // If schemaless (r12 == 0), reset RBC per-file offset before
        // the inner loop; if schema-declared, no reset needed.
        cmp r12, 0;
        jne cd_schema_inner_head;
        call rbc_reset;

      cd_schema_inner_head:
        // file_read_chunk(handle, fr_chunk_buf, CHUNK_MAX)
        mov rdi, rbx;
        lea rsi, [rip + fr_chunk_buf];
        mov rdx, 65536;                 // CHUNK_MAX
        call file_read_chunk;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je cd_file_close;               // 0 bytes = EOF this file

        // Dispatch on schema-ness (r12 preserved across the read).
        cmp r12, 0;
        je cd_schema_rbc_call;

        // ---- M3-001: pipe_forward_write(hash_ptr, chunk, bytes) ------
        mov rdx, rax;                   // bytes read (arg3: total_len)
        mov rdi, r12;                   // hash_ptr
        lea rsi, [rip + fr_chunk_buf];  // src
        call pipe_forward_write;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne cd_system_error;
        jmp cd_schema_inner_head;

      cd_schema_rbc_call:
        // ---- M3-002: rbc_emit_chunk(chunk, bytes) --------------------
        mov rsi, rax;                   // bytes read (arg2: len)
        lea rdi, [rip + fr_chunk_buf];  // src
        call rbc_emit_chunk;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne cd_system_error;
        jmp cd_schema_inner_head;

        // ==============================================================
        //   M2 render-text path (FLAG_SCHEMA clear)
        // ==============================================================
      cd_file_render_path:
      cd_file_inner_head:
        // file_read_chunk(handle, fr_chunk_buf, CHUNK_MAX)
        mov rdi, rbx;                   // handle
        lea rsi, [rip + fr_chunk_buf];  // dst
        mov rdx, 65536;                 // CHUNK_MAX
        call file_read_chunk;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je cd_file_close;               // 0 bytes = EOF

        // render_write_bytes(fr_chunk_buf, bytes)
        lea rdi, [rip + fr_chunk_buf];
        mov rsi, rax;                   // bytes read
        call render_write_bytes;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne cd_system_error;
        jmp cd_file_inner_head;

      cd_file_close:
        // file_close(handle) — M2 no-op; return ignored.
        mov rdi, rbx;
        call file_close;

        add r14, 1;
        jmp cd_file_outer_head;

        // ==============================================================
        //   Stdin path (M2-004 streaming stdin passthrough)
        // ==============================================================
      cd_stdin_path:
      cd_stdin_head:
        // stdin_read_chunk(fr_chunk_buf, CHUNK_MAX)
        lea rdi, [rip + fr_chunk_buf];
        mov rsi, 65536;                 // CHUNK_MAX
        call stdin_read_chunk;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je cd_ok;                       // 0 = EOF

        // render_write_bytes(fr_chunk_buf, bytes)
        lea rdi, [rip + fr_chunk_buf];
        mov rsi, rax;
        call render_write_bytes;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne cd_system_error;
        jmp cd_stdin_head;

        // ==============================================================
        //   Exit code assembly + epilogue
        // ==============================================================
      cd_ok:
        xor rax, rax;
        jmp cd_epilogue;

      cd_system_error:
        mov rax, 3;
        jmp cd_epilogue;

      cd_usage_error:
        mov rax, 2;
        jmp cd_epilogue;

      cd_cap_denied:
        mov rax, 4;

      cd_epilogue:
        pop r15;
        pop r14;
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret;
      }
    }

  // ============================================================================
  // cat_dispatch_from_buf(buf, buf_len) -> exit_code
  //
  // Signature: cat_dispatch_from_buf : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{}
  //   RDI: buf ptr
  //   RSI: byte count
  //   RAX: 0 on OK, 3 on sink overflow
  //
  // Alt entry preserved from M1-003 for the raw bytes-through-sink
  // test harness. Bypasses argv, file read, AND the render layer —
  // drives `tty_write_bytes` directly. Used by pre-M2 fixtures + as
  // a smoke check that tty_write_bytes' 64-KiB M2 cap is honoured.
  //
  // The M2 render pipeline is exercised via `cat_dispatch` with a
  // pre-seeded FileRead::seed table (see file header).
  //
  // Register plan (3-push callee-save + pad; unchanged from M1):
  //   r12 = buf
  //   r13 = buf_len
  //   r14 = pad
  // ============================================================================
  pub let cat_dispatch_from_buf : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (buf: u64) (buf_len: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "cat.M1-003 cat_dispatch_from_buf. Alt entry preserved through M2: drives TtySink::tty_write_bytes directly, bypassing argv + file read + render. Useful for smoke-checking the M2 65536-byte sink cap and as a pre-shell.M4 bytes-through-sink harness. 3-push prologue (r12 / r13 / r14 as pad) — entry rsp%16 == 8 (post-CALL); +3*8 = 24; (8 + 24) mod 16 = 0 → nested call site aligned. r12/r13 preserve buf/buf_len across the tty_reset call which is free to clobber caller-save regs.",
      block: {
        push r12;
        push r13;
        push r14;

        mov r12, rdi;
        mov r13, rsi;

        call tty_reset;

        mov rdi, r12;
        mov rsi, r13;
        call tty_write_bytes;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne cat_disp_buf_system_error;

        xor rax, rax;
        jmp cat_disp_buf_epilogue;

      cat_disp_buf_system_error:
        mov rax, 3;

      cat_disp_buf_epilogue:
        pop r14;
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        ret;
      }
    }
}
